,"open_issues":245,"watchers":17046,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/pulls/2117","html_url":"https://github.com/less/less.js/pull/2117","diff_url":"https://github.com/less/less.js/pull/2117.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/less/less.js/pull/2117.patch","merged_at":"2014-07-27T09:57:25Z"},"body":"The genCss method of ruleset.js splits child nodes into two groups:\n- rules,\n- rulesets.\n\nRules are always printed first and have special handling for last rule.\nRulesets are always printed second. Wrong ordering was caused by the\ncondition that determined what is rule and what is ruleset.\n\nIssue #2013: The condition made no difference between @charset and @page,\nbecause both are compiled into tree.Directive nodes. I added isRulesetLike\nmethod to the tree.Directive to differentiate between them.\n\nIssue #1954: The condition treated all tree.Anonymous types as rules and\ncaused them to float up. That is incorrect, because `@import (inline)` is\ncompiled into tree.Anonymous too, but should be treated as ruleset and\nstay where it is.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/2117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/2117/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":145782808,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE0NTc4MjgwOA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/events/145782808","actor":{"login":"SomMeri","id":618879,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxODg3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/618879?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri","html_url":"https://github.com/SomMeri","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/followers","following